 "Survey Advisor ⊣ Water Infrastructure Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A water-infrastructure
 leak-detection SURVEY COORDINATION actor -- not direct valve/main
 control authority and not a water-utility regulatory compliance
 authority. Four ops (`:log-pipe-condition` / `:leak-survey` /
 `:schedule-repair-recommendation` / `:escalate-critical-leak`), all
 `:effect :propose` only. Ten concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct valve/main
 control), permanent valve-actuate block, sensor-grounded
 CONFIRMED/NO-LEAK verdicts (leaksurvey.telemetry/grounds-verdict?,
 requiring cited readings to cover both acoustic-signature and
 pressure-differential metrics -- never advisor self-attestation),
 independent segment verification/registration before repair
 recommendation, independent on-file confirmed-leak verification
 before repair recommendation, double-recommendation guard, pipe-
 material validation, and flow-loss plausibility validation.
 Critical-leak escalation ALWAYS escalates to a human survey
 coordinator; `:log-pipe-condition` is the only op eligible to
 auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean. 74 tests / 202
 assertions green, clj-kondo 0 errors."}
